# BAKE_ROM: bake rom/rom.hex into the bitstream (personal build with the ROM
# present).  rtl/rom_banks.sv uses `ifdef BAKE_ROM`, which tests whether the
# macro is DEFINED -- NOT its value.  So "BAKE_ROM=0" STILL bakes the ROM in!
# For a ROM-free public build the line must be COMMENTED OUT / absent entirely
# (as below).  Uncomment it only for a personal baked build with rom.hex present.
# see rtl/rom_banks.sv and scripts/rom_bin2hex.py.
# set_global_assignment -name VERILOG_MACRO "BAKE_ROM=1"

